Requirements: 4   with obligations: 4

[task-01] A fresh `pip install -e .` must resolve a litellm release with which a
    recording run works. The litellm requirement in `pyproject.toml` is bounded on both
    sides, to a range of releases that install and that can build a model response, and
    the bound carries a comment saying why each side is where it is, so that the next
    person widening it knows what to re-check.
    -> litellm-release-works-with-recording-run  [functional/explicit]
       A fresh `pip install -e .` resolves a litellm release with which a recording run
       works.
    -> litellm-requirement-bounded-both-sides  [docs_config/explicit]
       The litellm requirement in `pyproject.toml` is bounded on both sides.
    -> litellm-installable-release-range  [compatibility/explicit]
       Constrain the litellm dependency to a range of releases that install.
    -> litellm-can-build-model-response  [functional/explicit]
       The selected litellm release can build a model response.
    -> litellm-bound-comment-justification  [docs_config/explicit]
       The litellm version bound in pyproject.toml includes comments explaining why the
       lower and upper sides are set where they are.

[task-02] The test suite includes a smoke test, which is itself a deliverable, that
    drives litellm's own completion path against the installed version far enough to
    build its response model, without contacting a provider. It runs in the ordinary
    replay-mode suite, so CI fails when an installed litellm cannot construct a
    response.
    -> smoke-test-included  [test_demand/explicit]
       The test suite includes a smoke test.
    -> litellm-completion-path-builds-response-model  [functional/explicit]
       litellm's own completion path against the installed version drives far enough to
       build its response model.
    -> no-provider-contact  [compatibility/explicit]
       The change does not contact a provider.
    -> ordinary-replay-mode-suite  [functional/explicit]
       The smoke test runs in the ordinary replay-mode suite.
    -> ci-fails-on-response-construction-failure  [functional/explicit]
       CI fails when an installed litellm cannot construct a response.
